  "question": {
    "text": "On charging the lead storage battery, the oxidation state of lead changes from $x_1$ to $y_1$ at the anode and from $x_2$ to $y_2$ at the cathode. The values of $x_1, y_1, x_2, y_2$ are respectively :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TyAnL",
      "text": "$+4,+2,0,+2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HJ74g",
      "text": "$+2,0,+2,+4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gzuZi",
      "text": "$0,+2,+4,+2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "u9FUp",
      "text": "$+2,0,0,+4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For charging of lead storage battery cell reaction is $2 \\mathrm{PbSO}_4(\\mathrm{~s})+2 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Pb}(\\mathrm{s})+\\mathrm{PbO}_2(\\mathrm{~s})+2 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4(\\mathrm{aq})$ At anode $\\mathrm{PbSO}_4$ reduced back to Pb and at cathode $\\mathrm{PbSO}_4$ oxidised back to $\\mathrm{PbO}_2$.<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& \\because \\quad \\mathrm{x}_1=+2, \\mathrm{y}_1=0 \\\\<br>& \\mathrm{x}_2=+2, \\mathrm{y}_2=4<br />\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
